      "original_context": {
        "full_target": "Let \\(n,m\\geq1\\) be integers and let\n\\(u:\\mathbb R^n\\times(0,\\infty)\\to\\mathbb R^m\\) be jointly smooth.\nFix \\(q\\in\\mathbb R^m\\) with \\(|q|=1\\). Assume:\n\n1. \\(|u(x,t)|=1\\) for all \\(x\\) and \\(t>0\\).\n2. The acceleration \\(u_{tt}-\\Delta_xu\\) is normal to the sphere at\n   \\(u\\): at each point there is a real scalar \\(a(x,t)\\) with\n   \\(u_{tt}-\\Delta_xu=a u\\). No regularity of the selected scalar is\n   assumed.\n3. For every \\(0<s<t<\\infty\\), a compact set\n   \\(C_{[s,t]}\\subset\\mathbb R^n\\) exists such that \\(u(x,r)=q\\) for\n   \\(x\\notin C_{[s,t]}\\), \\(r\\in[s,t]\\).\n\nWith Euclidean norms and Lebesgue measure, define\n\n\\[\ne(x,t)=|u_t(x,t)|^2+\\sum_{j=1}^n|\\partial_{x_j}u(x,t)|^2,\n\\qquad E(t)=\\int_{\\mathbb R^n}e(x,t)\\,dx.\n\\]\n\nThe spatial gradient square is the Frobenius square, and\n\\(\\Delta_xu=\\sum_j\\partial_{x_jx_j}u\\) component by component.\nProve integrability of \\(e(\\cdot,t)\\), differentiability of \\(E\\),\nand \\(E'(t)=0\\) for every \\(t>0\\). No assertion at time zero is required.",
        "hypotheses": [
          {
            "id": "H001",
            "statement": "n≥1 and m≥1.",
            "origin": "problem.md:25"
          },
          {
            "id": "H002",
            "statement": "u:ℝ^n × (0,∞) → ℝ^m is jointly C^∞ (smooth) on this open domain.",
            "origin": "problem.md:25-26"
          },
          {
            "id": "H003",
            "statement": "|q|=1.",
            "origin": "problem.md:27"
          },
          {
            "id": "H004",
            "statement": "For every x∈ℝ^n and every t>0, |u(x,t)|=1.",
            "origin": "problem.md:29"
          },
          {
            "id": "H005",
            "statement": "For every x∈ℝ^n and every t>0 there exists a real scalar a such that u_tt(x,t)−Δ_xu(x,t)=a u(x,t). No regularity of a selected scalar field is assumed.",
            "origin": "problem.md:30-33"
          },
          {
            "id": "H006",
            "statement": "For every pair of real times 0<s<t<∞ there exists a compact C⊂ℝ^n such that u(x,r)=q for every x∉C and every r∈[s,t].",
            "origin": "problem.md:34-36"
          }
        ],
        "conclusion": "For every t>0, e(·,t) is absolutely Lebesgue integrable on ℝ^n, E is differentiable at t, and E'(t)=0. In addition E(s)=E(t) for all s,t>0; no assertion at time zero is made."
      },
